    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e834e1312d54ef0ab70549d3883c0c6",
      "statement": "The CLI export and import subcommands do not implement file logic; cmd_export delegates to sync.exporter.export_to_json/export_to_markdown and cmd_import delegates to sync.importer.import_from_json. This is the reason the cli->sync dependency edge exists.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/cli/commands.py#L44-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d01a3babaf97a05955a036845f98852921900a4b373f74936dba4829a70f411c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_431068511b554247a45d3243654c2219",
      "statement": "Store is the single JSON-backed persistence abstraction shared by all three interface domains. Every mutating operation is a full load->modify->save cycle with no in-memory caching and no locking; add() loads all bookmarks, appends one, and writes the whole list back; remove() loads, filters, and writes back, so concurrent writers can overwrite each other's changes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/store.py#L43-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cce70956d0c1ad685c65b3994ddb0777d915840ff887f6b42dfec30f7af3eb3e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2f23e0b0b3e442af840f8a7d751d7cf5",
      "statement": "linkkeep/api/deps.py holds a module-level singleton Store (_store_singleton) lazily initialized on the first get_store() call and reused for all subsequent requests. The singleton caches the Store object (its resolved path), not the bookmark data; each operation still reads/writes the JSON file. reset_store_singleton() exists for test isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/api/deps.py#L4-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc0d7af12dd6b76b934e15905cdc7f9a8c05f6155a2996183e377165aee4dbdd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21fb51ffe5014279abc698ea1948b658",
      "statement": "Bookmarks are persisted as a JSON array at ~/.linkkeep/bookmarks.json by default; the storage directory is overridable via the LINKKEEP_HOME environment variable, resolved by Store._home().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/store.py#L10-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6cad820cc1ae544fc0baa2324c16138efcdcfd1e73140c2d544d35e80b4c427b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8878c3875f8142ed96a8ac8347007a8a",
      "statement": "The wired CLI subcommands registered in build_parser() are: add, list, remove, count, export, import, and tag-overlap. A cmd_top_tags handler exists in commands.py but build_parser registers no top-tags subparser, so it is unreachable from the linkkeep entry point. README is stale: it lists only the original six subcommands and omits the wired tag-overlap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L10-L12",
